{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519876-a-surprisingly-good-reason-against-infernalism-courtesy-of-tremere","id":1519876,"title":"A surprisingly good reason against Infernalism, courtesy of Tremere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-05T09:53:24-07:00","id":1519876,"title":"A surprisingly good reason against Infernalism, courtesy of Tremere","content":"A while back I was going through the whitewolf wiki like usual and happened to find myself on the page for <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/House_Tremere\" target=\"_blank\">House Tremere</a> from Ars Magica and Dark Ages. Reading through the page, I ended up finding this nugget of wisdom.<br /> <br /> \u201cUnlike some of the more venturesome Tytali, the Tremere held a contempt against dealing with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Demon_(WOD)\" target=\"_blank\">demons</a>. A demon that was weak enough to be dominated would not be powerful to fulfill tasks that were worthy of the trouble involved. A demon that was powerful enough to grant boons, in turn, could never be dominated or enslaved, there would always be a loophole that the creature would exploit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Now the traditional arguments given for why you shouldn't be making deals with demons tend to come down to your soul being damned to hell for all eternity, and becoming a pawn for your new master. Now don't get me wrong, eternal damnation and servitude to a demon is good reason enough not to deal with forces that have existed millennia longer than you have. But never have I seen an explanation like this. Compared to other arguments against infernalism, this one sounds almost business-like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T14:13:17-07:00","id":1519900,"title":"","content":"Given what we know of the Tremere, I'd say it's not surprising the &quot;but your soul will be damned for eternity!&quot; line of argument doesn't really sway them.<br /> <br /> Mages also tend to have a more nuanced view of the spirit world than anyone else; what is a &quot;demon&quot; but a particular class of spirit? In <i>particular </i>a class of spirit you probably don't have any moral qualms about enslaving or imprisoning, since your local definition of &quot;demon&quot; it almost <i>certainly </i>includes &quot;deserving of whatever bad stuff befalls it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would stop short of calling it &quot;businesslike&quot;, though; a businesslike argument would say that weak demons can still be at least more situationally useful than a mortal servant, so ROI might still be positive. A powerful demon carries risks, but a risk-benefit assessment might still say it's worth it depending on the context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T15:42:47-07:00","id":1519905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1519876-a-surprisingly-good-reason-against-infernalism-courtesy-of-tremere?p=1519900#post1519900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given what we know of the Tremere, I'd say it's not surprising the &quot;but your soul will be damned for eternity!&quot; line of argument doesn't really sway them.<br /> <br /> Mages also tend to have a more nuanced view of the spirit world than anyone else; what is a &quot;demon&quot; but a particular class of spirit? In <i>particular </i>a class of spirit you probably don't have any moral qualms about enslaving or imprisoning, since your local definition of &quot;demon&quot; it almost <i>certainly </i>includes &quot;deserving of whatever bad stuff befalls it&quot;.<br /> <br /> I would stop short of calling it &quot;businesslike&quot;, though; a businesslike argument would say that weak demons can still be at least more situationally useful than a mortal servant, so ROI might still be positive. A powerful demon carries risks, but a risk-benefit assessment might still say it's worth it depending on the context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got to say, never really thought of it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}